{"qid":"Q1473253","names":["French Mandate for Syria and Lebanon"],"title":"French Mandate for Syria and Lebanon","endonym":null,"capsule":"The French Mandate for Syria and the Lebanon was a League of Nations mandate established in 1920 after the partition of the Ottoman Empire, placing the territories of present-day Syria and Lebanon under French administration. France reorganized the region into several states, including the State of Greater Lebanon proclaimed in 1920. The mandate ended with the independence of Syria and Lebanon in the 1940s.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. This polity has not yet received individual source review: treat extents as indicative atlas convention.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[],"britannica":null,"cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Mandate for Syria and the Lebanon","rulers":[{"qid":null,"name":"Henri Gouraud","nativeName":"Henri Gouraud","roman":"Henri Gouraud","start":1919,"end":1923,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Maxime Weygand","nativeName":"Maxime Weygand","roman":"Maxime Weygand","start":1923,"end":1924,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Maurice Sarrail","nativeName":"Maurice Sarrail","roman":"Maurice Sarrail","start":1924,"end":1925,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Henry de Jouvenel","nativeName":"Henry de Jouvenel","roman":"Henry de Jouvenel","start":1925,"end":1926,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Auguste Henri Ponsot","nativeName":"Auguste Henri Ponsot","roman":"Auguste Henri Ponsot","start":1926,"end":1933,"image":null,"imageU